branch: the-memory-counter-measures-what-it-claims

kq's two cost goldens retire bytes_peak and gain held_peak_bytes, and what it
buys is a counter that reports the memory kq actually holds: 336,956 bytes
where the old name said 26,298. Nothing kq allocates changes and every other
counter in both files is byte-identical.

The gain is that the objective could not see this memory at all. kanso's own
corpus had eleven fixtures reporting zero held bytes while holding some, which
is how a leak fix landed and moved welfare by nothing.
